course: dictionary
lesson: 2622
title: Describing things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To describe something is to tell someone what it is like: how it looks, sounds, feels, smells or behaves. When you describe, you give clues so the listener can picture it. «The castle had tall grey towers and a red door» describes the castle; «The castle was there» does not.
explain: You can also describe what happened, step by step, like telling a story in order. Scientists describe what they saw in an experiment, and in maths you describe shapes by their sides, corners and patterns.
explain: Describe is a verb, so it changes: describes, described, describing. A description is the noun, the thing you have written or said. Descriptive is an adjective, so a descriptive word helps someone picture something clearly.
fact: Describe means to say or write what someone or something is like.
fact: Describe can also mean to tell what happened, step by step.
fact: In maths, to describe a shape means to say its sides, corners or symmetry.
fact: «The Ukrainian constitution describes the flag as two equal stripes, blue above and yellow below.»
fact: «If you do not know the address, you describe landmarks such as shops, signs or parks.»
exercise: «The Ukrainian constitution describes the flag as two equal stripes, blue above and yellow below.» What does the constitution say the flag is like? | Red with a white star | Three thin black lines | Green with a yellow moon | *Two equal stripes, blue above and yellow below
exercise: You are lost and do not know the address. What can you describe to help the police find you? | *Landmarks such as shops, signs or parks | The song you listened to in the car | Your favourite pudding | Nothing, so just wait quietly
exercise: In maths, what does it mean to describe a square? | A round shape with no corners | Two long lines that never meet | *Its four equal sides and four corners | Its colour and its size only
test: «Her new bike was described as sleek and silver.» What does described mean here? | *Told what it was like | Hidden under a cover | Broken into pieces | Sold for money
test: Which word is the noun form of describe? | *description | describes | dreary | described
exam: Lily must tell the police what the thief looked like. Which is the best description? | He ran fast | He was caught yesterday | *He wore a red cap, a torn green coat and had a limp | He was in the park
